{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3078","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3078","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3078\",\"parent_revision\":\"73bf55bfb293941299b9c4b569a57a1bc0bcf1e813b926f6391a1bb2d9ac7dcc\",\"root_revision\":\"73bf55bfb293941299b9c4b569a57a1bc0bcf1e813b926f6391a1bb2d9ac7dcc\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nVerified by direct code reading (dispatched to check the artifact-ownership split claimed in\\n`docs/component-architecture.md`): `backlog_core/server.py`'s `artifact_read()` calls the\\nstorage provider's `get_content()` directly and returns raw content. `progressive_markdown`\\n(the R1 engine) has zero involvement \u2014 no parsing, no navigation, no pagination, no content\\nidentity (R8).\\n\\nThis is the same \\\"second implementation\\\" pattern R1 already forbids for item/plan/task reads\\n(#3057, #3058), just for a different operation. Artifact content can be large \u2014 architecture\\nspecs and codebase analyses are named examples in the contract's Scope section \u2014 and today it\\nreturns unbounded, with none of R2/R7/R8 applied.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `artifact_read()` (and its transports) route content through the markdown engine\\n- [ ] Artifact content over budget returns the compact form and paginates like any other\\n      markdown source (R2, R3)\\n- [ ] Artifact content carries an R8 content identity like any other paginated response\\n- [ ] No component outside the engine parses, windows, or truncates artifact content\\n</div>\\n\\n## Relationship To 3055\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nDistinct bug. #3055 is about a manifest entry reporting `current` status when its content was\\nnever durably written \u2014 a registration/durability defect. This issue is about the delivery\\npath for artifacts whose content *does* exist and *can* be read \u2014 it just doesn't go through\\nthe engine when it is. Fixing #3055 does not fix this, and fixing this does not fix #3055.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"913612d827306f9ec48008473571ad47062e827f04c722f0717f22aa3592c21c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvb9ow\"}"}